  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "So, you're wondering about the timeline for a kitchen backsplash? It's not usually an overnight job, and a lot of it comes down to cure times. Generally, a standard backsplash install can take anywhere from one to three days from start to finish. Day one might involve prep, layout, and setting the tiles. Then comes the waiting game. Thinset, the adhesive that holds your tiles, typically needs about 24 hours to cure before you can even think about grouting. If you jump the gun, you risk your tiles shifting or the grout not adhering properly. Once the thinset is cured and you've applied the grout, that needs its own time to dry and harden, which can be another 24 hours to three days, or even longer depending on the specific product and humidity levels. Don't forget to factor in sealing the grout, too! If you're coordinating with other kitchen renovations, like new countertops, remember that countertops usually go in first, and some pros even suggest waiting a day after the countertop's epoxy has set before starting the backsplash. For a precise timeline and seamless coordination with your other projects, especially in the Denver area, it's always a good idea to chat with experts like HH Remodeling LLC. We can give you a realistic schedule and handle all the coordination."
    }
  ],
